# Simplification synthesis: Deployment-Time Machine Learning: LLM-Selected Updates Without a Single Score

The core claim is findable, and the sections serve it. The available gains come from making the bet's statement single and early, giving its mechanism one clean statement, and trimming precedents to their roles. Most other findings are local and fall inside these three.

## Opportunities

### 1. One statement of the bet, stated up front

- Location: introduction, from "The case argued here is the one where the changes are edits" through "Whether spending more computation on that work yields better decisions is a further test", together with the bolded bet in "Proof, formula, judgment" ("We bet that a fixed-weight language model can do that work autonomously…").
- Combines: core-claim-obscured (all three findings); marginal-value-redundancy ("The loop itself is not new.").
- Preserve or decide: The two versions of the bet differ in content, not just wording. The later one adds "decide the cases it leaves open" and states that the declared objective stays fixed. The author must choose which scope is the article's bet before the two are aligned. The novelty disclaimer may be load-bearing: it moves the claimed novelty from the loop to the judge. If it moves out of the opening, the opening should still mark that the bet concerns the judge. The scope restriction to readable, addressable stores bounds the article's claim and should stay visible early, even if shortened.

### 2. Consolidate the robust-comparison mechanism and the judge's job

- Location: "Proof, formula, judgment", from "**Robust comparison.**" through "such cycles are something a test can look for", plus "Letting a change stand while its verdict is open is a decision, not a demonstrated gain" in the success section.
- Combines: detail-overhang (stochastic dominance / preference-model duplication); marginal-value-redundancy ("The procedure need not assign every version a number…" paragraph).
- Preserve or decide: Keep these points, which are substantive and appear only here. In open-ended work an objection can add a criterion and widen the set. The article's relation is stricter than the method's "at least as good". Changing the alternative can close an open comparison, as with a trial and a cheap way back. Consistent answers can still neglect a required cost. Cycles are testable. The author decides whether stochastic dominance stays as the familiar entry point or the decision-analysis method alone carries the rule. The "possible" preference definition is never used again, so it can go unless a companion article depends on it. One point is structural: "Robust comparison" is bolded as a fourth item after three historical precedents, but it is the bet's mechanism, not a precedent. The author may want to mark that change of role.

### 3. Reduce precedent and source paragraphs to their argumentative role

- Location: the "**Formal proof.**" paragraph in "Proof, formula, judgment", and the Harness Evolution paragraph in "Compatible with the Bitter Lesson".
- Combines: detail-overhang (Gödel machine; Harness Evolution, INFO); marginal-value-redundancy (Gödel closing recap); branch-bloat (Harness Evolution, INFO).
